s": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Eldest", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "eldest"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q308982", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eldest"], "tags": ["literary work", "Novels & Prose Fiction", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Eldest contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": ""Eldest" played a pivotal role in shaping the modern landscape of young adult fantasy literature, influencing countless authors and contributing to a cultural movement that revitalized interest in the genre.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-01T01:34:04Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28487247073", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "2005 novel by christopher paolini Created by Christopher Paolini.", "newValue": ""Eldest," published in 2005, is the second book in the critically acclaimed "Inheritance Cycle" series written by Christopher Paolini, an American author who began the series at the age of fifteen. The book continues the epic narrative set in the fictional land of Alagaësia, detailing the adventures of the protagonist, Eragon, and his dragon, Saphira, as they confront the dark forces threatening their world. The series, which includes "Eragon," "Eldest," and subsequent titles, has garnered a global readership and has significantly contributed to the resurgence of the fantasy genre in contemporary literature.

The events in "Eldest" unfold in various locations across Alagaësia, most notably in the elven city of Ellesméra and the vast deserts of the Empire. The narrative introduces key characters, including the wise elf Oromis and the formidable antagonist Galbatorix, whose oppressive reign shapes the fate of the realm. The book explores themes of power, identity, and moral choices, as Eragon grapples with his responsibilities as a Dragon Rider and the complexities of his lineage. His journey not only reveals ancient secrets but also sets the stage for the climactic battles that define the series' overarching conflict.

